{% block content %}
<main id="main">
    <section class="page-header">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#fff;">FAQ</span>
        <h1>Questions, answered straight.</h1>
        <p>The things people call us about most. If yours isn't here, call (301) 252-3586 — we'll answer.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item" open>
            <summary>How fast can I get a dumpster?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">Most addresses in our core service area (Beltsville, Greenbelt, College Park, Laurel, Hyattsville) can be delivered the same day if you call before noon. Outside that radius, next-day is standard.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What size dumpster do I need?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">10 yard for garage cleanouts, 15 for single-room remodels, 20 for whole-house cleanouts (our most popular), 25 for additions, and 30 for full demolitions or large construction. Call us — we'll help you pick the right one.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How much does it cost?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">Pricing is per material and per size. Construction debris runs from $550 for a 10-yard up to $665 for a 30-yard, and every rental includes 14 days, delivery, and pickup with a per-size tonnage allowance. It's not flat-rate — excess weight beyond your allowance is $105 per additional ton. Every quote is in writing, so you'll know the base price and the overage rate before you book.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What can I put in the dumpster?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">Most construction, demo, household, and yard debris. We can't take: hazardous waste (paints, solvents, oils), tires, batteries, refrigerators with refrigerant, propane tanks, or asbestos. Ask if you're unsure — we'll point you to the right disposal.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do I need a permit?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">Permits are only needed if the dumpster sits in the street or public right-of-way. Most driveways and private lots are permit-free. Each city handles it differently — we'll help you figure it out for your address.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How long can I keep the dumpster?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">Standard rental is 14 days, with delivery and pickup included. Need more? Day extensions are inexpensive — just call. Pickup is on request — call to schedule when you're ready and we'll come get it.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Will the dumpster damage my driveway?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">No. Our drivers lay protective boards under the wheels and corner posts before setting the container down. We've delivered on asphalt, concrete, and pavers without issue. If you have a specialty surface, mention it when you book and we'll plan accordingly.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How heavy can I load it?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">Each size includes a tonnage allowance: 10yd = 1 ton, 15yd = 1.5 ton, 20yd = 2 ton, 25yd = 2 ton, 30yd = 3 ton. Excess weight beyond your allowance is billed at $105 per additional ton. Heavy debris (concrete, brick, dirt) has lower fill limits — call for guidance.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How much space do I need?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">For most sizes, allow about 22–24 feet of length and 10 feet of width plus overhead clearance (no low branches or wires). A 30-yard needs a longer run-up. We can walk you through your driveway photos if you're unsure.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do you offer Spanish-speaking service?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">Sí. Hablamos español en la oficina y atendemos solicitudes en español por teléfono y formulario. Llámanos al (301) 252-3586.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How do I pay?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">Credit card, debit card, ACH, check, or cash. Commercial accounts welcome — ask about billing. We email an invoice the day of delivery.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What if I need to cancel or reschedule?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">No problem — call at least 24 hours before delivery to reschedule or cancel without charge. Same-day cancellations may carry a trip fee depending on whether the truck has already been dispatched.</div>
          </details>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center" style="margin-top: var(--space-12);">
          <p class="lead" style="margin: 0 auto var(--space-5);">Still have questions?</p>
          <a href="tel:+13012523586" class="btn btn-lg">Call (301) 252-3586</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
